<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::diplomatic_engagement" target="france_euro_bond_crisis::sovereign_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in external diplomatic initiatives that de-escalate communications- and access-related disputes reduces the perceived likelihood of broader geopolitical spillovers to the EU, which lowers the additional premium investors charge for holding French sovereign debt.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">france_euro_bond_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::diplomatic_engagement" target="iran_gulf_standoff::crude_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater diplomatic engagement (deconfliction and negotiations) among external actors focused on communications-access and escalation management reduces the probability of hostile state or proxy actions against Gulf energy flows, lowering the risk premium embedded in crude prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
</edge>
