<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_risk" target="ai_market_cyber_instabil::cyber_exploit_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising propensity for tactical or strategic escalation motivates states and proxies to launch offensive cyber campaigns (including ransomware, intrusions, and supply‑chain attacks) that target adversary cloud and AI infrastructure, raising exploit frequency.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_market_cyber_instabil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_risk" target="france_euro_bond_crisis::contagion_transmission" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A higher risk of tactical or strategic escalation in the Russia–Ukraine war increases investors' tendency to reassess cross-border exposures, accelerating the speed and intensity with which financial stress or risk perceptions propagate between sovereign bond markets including France.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">france_euro_bond_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_risk" target="iran_gulf_standoff::insurance_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in escalation risk tied to the Russia–Ukraine war prompts global underwriters to reprice war/political-risk exposure and widen exclusions, causing insurers to raise premiums for coverage on maritime and energy shipments transiting the Gulf region.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_risk" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::chain_diversification" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A rising systemic risk of conflict escalation that could disrupt trade routes, component supplies, or trigger sanctions drives firms and policymakers to accelerate re‑routing of suppliers and sourcing away from concentrated producers tied into the conflict arena — including China‑centric nodes.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
