<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="ai_market_cyber_instabil::compute_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export controls legally block shipments of advanced accelerators and related datacenter components to targeted jurisdictions, directly reducing the deployable GPU/accelerator inventory and near-term datacenter provisioning in those markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_market_cyber_instabil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="ai_market_cyber_instabil::counterparty_concentrati" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Broad export restrictions remove a portion of the supplier pool from certain markets, leaving only a small set of approved vendors and thereby increasing concentration of critical AI hardware and service counterparties.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_market_cyber_instabil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="france_euro_bond_crisis::sovereign_bond_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export controls on advanced semiconductors and dual‑use components disrupt revenues and supply chains for French and EU tech exporters, weakening growth and increasing France's fiscal financing needs, which pushes long-term sovereign yields higher.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">france_euro_bond_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::private_net_access_contr" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger export controls on advanced communications and satellite components reduce competing supplier capacity (especially outside allied jurisdictions), concentrating service provision in a smaller set of private firms that can unilaterally throttle or cut access for users in the Russia–Ukraine theater.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
