<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::chain_diversification" target="ai_market_cyber_instabil::counterparty_concentrati" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Corporate and policy-driven supplier re‑selection and multi-sourcing contracts directly reduce reliance on single providers or locations, lowering counterparty concentration in AI infrastructure and services.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_market_cyber_instabil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::chain_diversification" target="iran_gulf_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Accelerated re-routing of supply chains away from China increases commercial traffic and chokepoint transits through the Persian Gulf, raising target density and the tactical utility of interdiction by Iran-linked actors, thereby increasing the frequency of maritime attacks.</data>
