<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" target="ai_market_cyber_instabil::cyber_exploit_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in kinetic attacks and proxy operations in the Gulf typically coincides with or triggers parallel state and nonstate cyber campaigns against shipping, logistics providers and related infrastructure, raising the overall rate of cyber exploits including against AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_market_cyber_instabil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" target="france_euro_bond_crisis::contagion_transmission" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharp uptick in attacks increases global risk aversion and prompts synchronized selling and margin calls across sovereign bond books, accelerating the speed and intensity with which stress spreads into French and other euro-area debt markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">france_euro_bond_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::foreign_perceived_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained uptick in attacks on commercial shipping directly raises foreign firms' and governments' perceptions that overseas economic and technological engagement faces acute physical and geopolitical hazards, increasing the intensity of perceived security risk tied to cross-border tech ties.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
