</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::insurance_premium" target="iran_gulf_standoff::investor_risk_aversion" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::insurance_premium" target="ai_market_cyber_instabil::ai_capital_availability" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising war/political‑risk insurance premia raise operating costs and lower expected returns for firms building AI infrastructure (and for funds underwriting those builds), causing financiers to trim exposure to new AI deployments and slowing capital flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_market_cyber_instabil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::insurance_premium" target="france_euro_bond_crisis::sovereign_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising maritime insurance premia act as a market signal of elevated geopolitical and trade risk, leading investors to widen credit spreads and demand a higher risk premium on French sovereign debt to compensate for deteriorating external trade and fiscal outlooks.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">france_euro_bond_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::insurance_premium" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::chain_diversification" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising war/political-risk insurance premiums for Gulf routes make logistics and inventory more expensive and volatile, prompting firms and purchasers to accelerate supplier and route diversification away from chokepoint-dependent sources.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::insurance_premium" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::outbound_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher insurance costs for maritime and energy-related projects directly raise the cost and perceived risk of overseas asset deployment, leading state and private investors to delay or reduce outbound investment flows into vulnerable logistics- or energy-dependent foreign assets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
