<edge source="ai_market_cyber_instabil::cyber_exploit_rate" target="france_euro_bond_crisis::sovereign_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A major cyberexploit that disrupts French payment, clearing, or central banking IT systems would sharply raise perceived default and political risk for France by interrupting market functioning and forcing emergency policy responses, so investors demand a higher sovereign risk premium.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_market_cyber_instabil</data>
  <data key="d39">france_euro_bond_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_market_cyber_instabil::cyber_exploit_rate" target="iran_gulf_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in cyber exploits against shipping systems (AIS, ECDIS, satellite comms or port OT) enables state/proxy actors or criminals to blind, redirect or disable vessels and port defenses, lowering the cost and success rate of hostile actions and thus increasing the frequency/severity of maritime attacks.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_market_cyber_instabil</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_market_cyber_instabil::cyber_exploit_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::private_net_access_contr" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in cyber exploits against commercial networks prompt providers to implement emergency access restrictions, filtering, and geo-blocking to contain attacks, thereby increasing private operators' effective control of who can connect and under what terms.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_market_cyber_instabil</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
