<edge source="france_euro_bond_crisis::sovereign_risk_premium" target="ai_market_cyber_instabil::ai_capital_availability" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharp rise in sovereign risk premia increases banks' and institutional investors' funding costs and regulatory capital charges for exposures in the affected jurisdiction, prompting immediate cuts to venture debt, corporate lending lines and risk allocations to AI projects and thus reducing available investable capital for AI buildout.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">france_euro_bond_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_market_cyber_instabil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="france_euro_bond_crisis::sovereign_risk_premium" target="iran_gulf_standoff::insurance_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in France's sovereign risk premium raises perceived systemic and counterparty risk for European insurers and reinsurers, prompting them to widen war/political-risk premiums for Gulf maritime and energy cargoes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">france_euro_bond_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="france_euro_bond_crisis::sovereign_risk_premium" target="russia_ukraine_war::domestic_polit_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A rising French sovereign risk premium raises government borrowing costs and forces visible fiscal retrenchment, which amplifies domestic scrutiny and partisan debate over expensive foreign commitments (including support to Ukraine), increasing political pressure.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">france_euro_bond_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="france_euro_bond_crisis::sovereign_risk_premium" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::outbound_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising French sovereign risk premia depress valuations and force European firms to sell noncore assets, creating near‑term acquisition opportunities that raise the pace and volume of Chinese outbound investments into European tech and industrial assets.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">france_euro_bond_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
